{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Understood — I'll keep this to a single question and then we go. I just need the one thing I can't infer: in one line, what is this project? (e.g. \"a web app to track my runs\", \"a CLI to rename files in bulk\", \"a REST API for a todo list\"). Give me that and I'll recommend a concrete stack, the thin proving slice, and file the foundation mission.","recommended":"One plain-language line naming what we're building"},"prd":"# Mission: <pending the captain's one-line description>\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up the project foundation — a running skeleton, a working test runner, and one thin vertical slice that proves they're connected.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- The project boots and shows something.\n- A real test runner is wired and a human can watch it run.\n- One thin vertical slice exercises skeleton + tests end to end.\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Building the product's actual features (each named feature is recorded and deferred to its own mission).\n**Constraints:**\n- Stack to be recommended once the captain names what we're building."}

